        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ann Beattie, Edgar Rice Burroughs, John Heard\n- Works: Chilly Scenes of Winter\n- Companies: Doubleday\n- Topics: American fiction writing, novels, short stories, film roles\n\nFacts:\n- Edgar Rice Burroughs was born on September 1, 1875, and he became an American fiction writer known for a prolific body of adventure and science-fiction work.\n- Ann Beattie was born on September 8, 1947, and she is an American novelist and short story writer.\n- Chilly Scenes of Winter is Ann Beattie’s first novel, and Doubleday published it in September 1976.\n- John Heard had a lead role in the film Chilly Scenes of Winter.\n- John Heard also had lead roles in Heart Beat, Cutter's Way, Cat People, C.H.U.D., and Deceived (1991).\n- John Heard had supporting roles in After Hours, Big, Beaches, Awakenings, Rambling Rose, The Pelican Brief, My Fellow Americans, Snake Eyes, and Animal Factory.",
